WEBVTT

00:00.140 --> 00:01.379
- [Instructor] Do some example,

00:01.379 --> 00:04.589
raising exponents or products of exponents

00:04.589 --> 00:05.866
to various powers,

00:05.866 --> 00:08.808
especially when we're dealing
with integer exponents.

00:08.808 --> 00:11.938
So let's say we have three
to the negative eight

00:11.938 --> 00:14.499
times seven to the third,

00:14.499 --> 00:17.611
and we wanna raise that
to the negative two power,

00:17.611 --> 00:19.266
and I want you to pause this video

00:19.266 --> 00:22.762
and see if you could
simplify this on your own.

00:22.762 --> 00:24.230
So the key realization here,

00:24.230 --> 00:26.174
there's couple of ways
that you can tackle it,

00:26.174 --> 00:27.770
but the key thing to realize

00:27.770 --> 00:29.728
is if you have the product of two things,

00:29.728 --> 00:33.788
and then you're raising that
to some type of a exponent,

00:33.788 --> 00:35.925
that is going to be the same thing

00:35.925 --> 00:39.350
as raising each of these
things to that exponent,

00:39.350 --> 00:40.946
and then taking the product.

00:40.946 --> 00:42.659
So this is going to be the same thing

00:42.659 --> 00:45.242
as three to the negative eight,

00:46.182 --> 00:49.659
and then that to the negative two

00:49.659 --> 00:54.167
times seven to the third
to the negative two,

00:54.167 --> 00:57.830
so I'll do seven to the
third right over here.

00:57.830 --> 00:59.409
And if I wanna simplify this,

00:59.409 --> 01:02.553
three to the negative
eight to the negative two,

01:02.553 --> 01:04.621
we have the other exponent property

01:04.621 --> 01:05.928
that if you're raising to an exponent

01:05.928 --> 01:08.157
and then raising that whole
thing to another exponent,

01:08.157 --> 01:10.087
then you can just multiply the exponents.

01:10.087 --> 01:13.338
So this is going to be
three to the negative eight

01:13.338 --> 01:16.119
times negative two power.

01:16.119 --> 01:17.860
Well, negative eight times negative two

01:17.860 --> 01:19.110
is positive 16,

01:20.229 --> 01:23.555
so this is gonna be
three to the 16th power

01:23.555 --> 01:24.994
right over there,

01:24.994 --> 01:26.438
and then this part right over here,

01:26.438 --> 01:28.657
seven to the third to the negative two.

01:28.657 --> 01:31.523
that's gonna be seven to the three

01:31.523 --> 01:33.226
times negative two,

01:33.226 --> 01:36.570
which is seven to the
negative sixth power.

01:36.570 --> 01:39.324
So that is seven to the negative six,

01:39.324 --> 01:43.512
and this would be about as
much as you could simplify.

01:43.512 --> 01:45.365
You could rewrite it different ways.

01:45.365 --> 01:47.377
Seven to the negative
six is the same thing

01:47.377 --> 01:49.688
as one over seven to the sixth,

01:49.688 --> 01:53.410
so you could write it
like three to the 16th.

01:53.410 --> 01:55.916
We'll use that same shade of blue,

01:55.916 --> 01:57.333
three to the 16th

01:58.738 --> 02:00.738
over seven to the sixth,

02:02.738 --> 02:05.027
but these two are equivalent,

02:05.027 --> 02:07.547
and there's other ways that
you could have tackled this.

02:07.547 --> 02:08.380
You could have said

02:08.380 --> 02:10.160
that this original thing right over here,

02:10.160 --> 02:12.458
this is the same thing as,

02:12.458 --> 02:13.579
three to the negative eight

02:13.579 --> 02:15.215
is the same thing as one
over three to the eighth,

02:15.215 --> 02:16.596
so you could have said
this is the same thing

02:16.596 --> 02:18.232
as seven to the third

02:18.232 --> 02:20.429
over three to the eighth,

02:20.429 --> 02:23.457
and then you're raising
that to the negative two,

02:23.457 --> 02:25.578
in which case you'd raise this
numerator to the negative two

02:25.578 --> 02:27.267
and the denominator to negative two,

02:27.267 --> 02:30.553
but you would have gotten
to the exact same place.

02:30.553 --> 02:33.053
Let's do another one of these.

02:34.854 --> 02:35.854
So let's say

02:40.147 --> 02:41.480
that we have got

02:46.300 --> 02:50.467
A to the negative two times
eight to the seventh power,

02:51.309 --> 02:54.967
and we wanna raise all of
that to the second power.

02:54.967 --> 02:57.430
Well, like before, I can
raise each of these things

02:57.430 --> 02:58.266
to the second power,

02:58.266 --> 03:01.697
so this is the same thing
as A to the negative two

03:01.697 --> 03:03.280
to the second power

03:04.280 --> 03:07.363
times this thing to the second power.

03:08.482 --> 03:11.919
Eight to the seventh to the second power,

03:11.919 --> 03:15.262
and then here, negative two
times two is negative four,

03:15.262 --> 03:18.512
so that's A to the negative four times,

03:19.663 --> 03:22.513
eight to the seven times two is 14,

03:22.513 --> 03:24.513
eight to the 14th power.

03:25.549 --> 03:27.279
In other videos, we go into more depth

03:27.279 --> 03:29.989
about why this should
hopefully make intuitive sense.

03:29.989 --> 03:31.327
Here you have eight to the seventh

03:31.327 --> 03:32.482
times eight to the seventh.

03:32.482 --> 03:34.351
Well, you would then
add the two exponents,

03:34.351 --> 03:35.889
and you would get to eight to the 14th,

03:35.889 --> 03:38.113
so however many times you
have eight to the seventh,

03:38.113 --> 03:40.528
you would just keep adding the exponents,

03:40.528 --> 03:44.295
or you would multiply by
seven that many times.

03:44.295 --> 03:46.141
Hopefully that didn't sound too confusing,

03:46.141 --> 03:48.341
but the general idea is if you
raise something to exponent

03:48.341 --> 03:49.495
and then another exponent,

03:49.495 --> 03:52.341
you can multiply those exponents.

03:52.341 --> 03:54.041
Let's do one more example

03:54.041 --> 03:56.863
where we are dealing with quotients,

03:56.863 --> 03:57.792
which that first example

03:57.792 --> 03:59.664
could have even been perceived as.

03:59.664 --> 04:01.331
So let's say we have

04:04.273 --> 04:06.106
two to the negative 10

04:07.299 --> 04:09.866
divided by four squared,

04:09.866 --> 04:13.140
and we're gonna raise all of
that to the seventh power.

04:13.140 --> 04:17.616
Well, this is equivalent
to two to the negative 10

04:17.616 --> 04:19.467
raised to the seventh power

04:19.467 --> 04:24.053
over four squared raised
to the seventh power,

04:24.053 --> 04:25.499
so if you have the
difference of two things

04:25.499 --> 04:27.322
and you're raising it to some power,

04:27.322 --> 04:28.789
that's the same thing as a numerator

04:28.789 --> 04:29.678
raised to that power

04:29.678 --> 04:32.621
divided by the denominator
raised to that power.

04:32.621 --> 04:35.228
Well, what's our numerator going to be?

04:35.228 --> 04:37.385
Well, we've done this drill before.

04:37.385 --> 04:40.836
It'd be two to the negative
10 times seventh power,

04:40.836 --> 04:44.742
so this would be equal to two
to the negative 70th power,

04:44.742 --> 04:47.294
and then in the denominator,

04:47.294 --> 04:48.344
four to the second power,

04:48.344 --> 04:50.032
then that raised to the seventh power.

04:50.032 --> 04:52.312
Well, two times seven is 14,

04:52.312 --> 04:54.560
so that's going to be four

04:54.560 --> 04:56.060
to the 17th power.

04:59.902 --> 05:01.884
Now, we actually could think

05:01.884 --> 05:04.681
about simplifying this even more.

05:04.681 --> 05:07.056
There's multiple ways that
you could rewrite this,

05:07.056 --> 05:08.821
but one thing you could
do is say, "Hey, look,

05:08.821 --> 05:11.236
"four is a power of two."

05:11.236 --> 05:13.192
So you could rewrite this as

05:13.192 --> 05:17.359
this is equal to two to the
negative 70th power over,

05:19.224 --> 05:22.724
instead of writing four to the 17th power,

05:24.436 --> 05:25.677
why did I write the 17th power?

05:25.677 --> 05:28.140
It should be four to the 14th power.

05:28.140 --> 05:29.533
Let me correct that.

05:29.533 --> 05:33.515
Instead of writing four to the 14th power,

05:33.515 --> 05:35.156
I instead could write,

05:35.156 --> 05:38.850
so this is two, get the colors right.

05:38.850 --> 05:42.017
This is two to the negative 70th over,

05:45.510 --> 05:46.718
instead of writing four,

05:46.718 --> 05:50.160
I could write two squared
to the 14th power.

05:50.160 --> 05:52.464
Four is the same thing as two squared,

05:52.464 --> 05:54.926
and so now I can rewrite this whole thing

05:54.926 --> 05:58.176
as two to the negative 70th power over,

06:00.069 --> 06:01.184
well, two to the second,

06:01.184 --> 06:02.609
and then that to the 14th,

06:02.609 --> 06:04.746
well, that's two to the 28th power,

06:04.746 --> 06:06.579
two to the 28th power.

06:09.282 --> 06:11.827
And so can I simplify this even more?

06:11.827 --> 06:13.032
Well, this is going to be equal

06:13.032 --> 06:14.199
to two to the,

06:16.735 --> 06:19.386
if I'm taking a quotient
with the same base,

06:19.386 --> 06:20.573
I can subtract the exponent.

06:20.573 --> 06:23.399
So it's gonna be negative 70.

06:23.399 --> 06:25.732
It's going to be negative 70

06:26.900 --> 06:29.150
minus 28th power, minus 28,

06:31.207 --> 06:33.417
and so this is going to simply

06:33.417 --> 06:36.000
two to the negative 98th power,

06:38.724 --> 06:42.891
and that's another way of
viewing the same expression.
